WEBVTT

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:15.667
What are we going to do?

00:00:54.542 --> 00:00:56.667
Stay out of sight until London.

00:00:57.458 --> 00:00:59.708
But... aren't you coming?

00:01:00.708 --> 00:01:04.500
I am too old and too tired
to go any further.

00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:07.500
Oh. Then, what will you do?

00:01:07.583 --> 00:01:10.917
Oh, don't you worry about me.

00:01:11.042 --> 00:01:14.167
I will be safe
in the home for retired bears.

00:01:14.292 --> 00:01:18.042
But it is not yet time
for you to retire.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.792
You must find a new home. In London.

00:01:21.917 --> 00:01:26.917
But... But I don't know anyone there.
What if they don't even like bears?

00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:32.792
You know, there was once a war
in the explorer's country.

00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:36.542
Thousands of children
were sent away for safety,

00:01:36.625 --> 00:01:40.458
left at railway stations
with labels around their necks,

00:01:40.542 --> 00:01:46.000
and unknown families took them in
and loved them like their own.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:50.417
They will not have forgotten
how to treat a stranger.

00:01:54.375 --> 00:01:58.292
Now take care, my darling.
Remember your manners.

00:01:59.792 --> 00:02:01.708
And keep safe.

00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:33.375
Hmm?

00:02:37.458 --> 00:02:38.875
Oh.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:58.583
Huh?

00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:17.917
OK, I'll just get it now.

00:03:19.583 --> 00:03:21.333
I'll throw it down.

00:03:22.833 --> 00:03:24.458
Hi.

00:04:05.375 --> 00:04:06.917
London.

00:04:08.542 --> 00:04:12.333
Oh, right. Yes.
Manners. Here goes.

00:04:12.542 --> 00:04:15.667
Good morning.
Really tipping it down, isn't it?

00:04:15.875 --> 00:04:17.125
Strange.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:19.500
How do you do?
I'm just looking for a home. And I...

00:04:21.958 --> 00:04:23.250
Hello?

00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:24.792
Excuse me...

00:04:25.542 --> 00:04:28.542
Does anyone know where I...
where I can find a home?

00:04:29.625 --> 00:04:30.708
Anyone?

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:43.500
Passengers are reminded to keep their
belongings with them at all times.

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:48.125
Unattended items will be taken away
and could be destroyed.

00:04:48.208 --> 00:04:49.458
Oh, dear.

00:04:49.542 --> 00:04:51.167
Oh, hello.

00:04:53.208 --> 00:04:54.250
You hungry?

00:04:55.625 --> 00:04:56.625
Me, too.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:01.500
But this is all I've got left.
It's really just for emergency.

00:05:04.417 --> 00:05:06.000
Oh, go on then.

00:05:12.083 --> 00:05:14.083
Ah, right, I see what I've done.

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:17.250
Erm, come on, you can't
all be having emergencies.

00:05:20.042 --> 00:05:23.458
Can you all just go away, please?
I need to look presentable.

00:05:23.542 --> 00:05:26.500
- That was so boring.
- I'm sorry you feel like that,

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:30.000
but it was my week to choose and I
enjoyed the Victorian Wool Experience.

00:05:30.083 --> 00:05:32.125
At least we spent time together
as a family.

00:05:32.208 --> 00:05:35.042
- And we learnt a lot about wool.
- Did you have fun, pumpkin?

00:05:35.083 --> 00:05:37.917
It's Judy, and it was fine
until you jumped in the lake.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.000
It's a bathing pond.
It's what you're supposed to do.

00:05:41.042 --> 00:05:43.750
- Not naked!
- Well, I forgot my costume.

00:05:43.792 --> 00:05:45.708
Jonathan, don't jump like that.

00:05:45.792 --> 00:05:48.583
Seven per cent of childhood accidents
start with jumping.

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:51.333
- If I'm gonna be an astronaut...
- You're not "gonna" be.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:53.333
You can be whatever you want, peanut.

00:05:53.417 --> 00:05:55.250
- Oh, stranger danger.
- What?

00:05:55.333 --> 00:05:58.167
Keep your eyes down.
There's some sort of bear over there.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.292
- Probably selling something.
- Good evening.

00:06:00.625 --> 00:06:02.125
No, thank you.

00:06:03.625 --> 00:06:04.708
Oh, dear.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:09.208
Must be doing something wrong.

